 186. We have gone through the evidence of PW 25 who was police officer of Lalbagh Police Station at the relevant time. Whose evidence has been discussed above. Where in it has been discussed that PW 25 at the instance of the Officer-in-Charge of Lalbagh Police Station. He came to the house of convict A Aziz who was former ward commissioner and defeated candidate of ward Commissioner's election held on 30-1-1994. He came their 10-20 AM before the occurrence took place. After arrival of the house convict A Aziz he found that 60/70 young person sat in their house. He also stated that he went their by getting information about the apprehension breach of peace due to election and on query from the convict A Aziz and his father about the situation. He was informed by the convict and his father that the men of Humayun Kabir used to beat their supporters in the Bazar. The PW 25 advised them to mention peace and he would see the matter then he went to the house of the informant. But he did not get the informant in his house. Then this PW 25 was returning back towards the office of the Panchayet. On the way of the office of Panchayet he was informed by 5/6 young peoples to the effect that the supporters of A Aziz are firing and blasting Cocktails. Thereafter he went to the Nababgonj Bazar; and from where he heard the sound of the firing. He further stated that he informed that matter to the OC for deploying forces. Subsequently the higher authority came to the place of occurrence along with the forces then the situation took controlled at about 12 hours on the said date. He also found the injured persons who have taken to the Hospital. He along with the other police officer came to the place of occurrence at Nababgonj road and arrested 5 persons under section 54 the Code of Criminal Procedure. This PW 25 is a police personnel but this material fact of the evidence was not denied by the defence. Therefore the evidence of PW 25 also carried a value to prove the strong circumstance that there was existing of apprehension breach of peace by the convict A Aziz and his supporters including convicts. It further presumed in his presence he heard that occurrence stated at the instance of the convict A Aziz and his supporters. This material fact is also corroborated and supported with the FIR as well as PW 1 along with other prosecution witnesses. In such view of the matter, we also find that the occurrence took place at the instance of convict A Aziz and his men only. 

